ification keys were bounded evidence mutations and were restored, with no verification residue remaining. The reboot was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol and showed acknowledged disruption and recovery. Final lifecycle observations show no failed services, no unexpected listeners, healthy package state, and only normal reboot-generated systemd temporary directories.","evidence_ids":["cmd-17c24a88413b4932","cmd-9f24c01018344e4e","cmd-c1d6e43e403b4185","cmd-dc1e1ac65e924c43","cmd-bd3782a8f5694f56","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, the reboot was acknowledged and observed as a bounded outage, a different post-restart boot ID was recorded, and system, sshd, account, key, policy, and live authentication behavior recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the reboot.","limitations":["The supplied public key's exact fingerprint and installation were verified, but a live login using that specific key pair could not be demonstrated because the corresponding private key was not part of the evidence. Live authentication was instead validated with temporary authorized test keys before and after reboot."]}
